Adapted source code
-------------------
Direction-arrow rendering (world + minimap arrows and arrow heads) and the
requirement display model are adapted from RuneLite Quest Helper:

    Quest Helper - https://github.com/Zoinkwiz/quest-helper
    Copyright (c) 2019-2024, Zoinkwiz and contributors
    Licensed under the BSD 2-Clause License

The original BSD 2-Clause copyright headers are retained in the adapted files.

Reference data
--------------
Some route steps carry precise NPC/object IDs and tile coordinates. These are
factual OSRS game data (not copyrightable) that were harvested at build time from
Quest Helper's open source (BSD 2-Clause, credited above) to save re-mapping
entities by hand. Quest Helper's own source code is NOT shipped in this plugin —
only the resulting factual IDs/coordinates are baked into the route data. The
build-time extractor lives in tools/data/ (qh_extract.py + qh_entities.json).

The expected NPC-dialogue options (which option to click) in
data/qh_dialogue.json were likewise harvested at build time from Quest Helper's
source (BSD 2-Clause, credited above); only the resulting option strings are
shipped as data, not Quest Helper's code. Extractor: tools/data/qh_dialogue.py.

Teleport data
-------------
data/teleports.json (teleport names, destinations and unlock requirements, for
the "fastest unlocked teleport" hint) was extracted from the Shortest Path plugin's
open-source transport data:

    Shortest Path - https://github.com/Skretzo/shortest-path
    Copyright (c) Skretzo and contributors
    Licensed under the BSD 2-Clause License

Only the resulting factual teleport data is shipped — none of Shortest Path's code
or its collision-map data. The plugin optionally drives an installed Shortest Path
instance over RuneLite's public plugin-message bus (no code dependency).

